  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian assistance to displaced populations and returnees in North Kivu, Democratic Republic of the Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) is grappling with a prolonged humanitarian crisis, exacerbated by the recent escalation of conflict in 2025 involving the March 23 Movement (M23). The M23&apos;s offensive in North and South Kivu provinces has resulted in widespread displacement, forced returns under harsh conditions, and significant infrastructural damage. The project aims to address the immediate and medium-term needs of crisis-affected communities through a multifaceted approach to alleviate human suffering while upholding the dignity and rights of all individuals impacted by the ongoing crisis.</narrative>
  </description>
